# Hermes MT5 WpfGuiController — deploy & paths

## Cause of “changes not visible”

1. **MetaEditor compiles from Program Files**, not from the git repo and not from AppData Terminal.
2. **`Assembly.LoadFrom` in MT5 caches assemblies** by identity — after UI changes bump `AssemblyName` + `ui_vN` folder + EA input path together (see `BuildInfo.Version`).
3. Chart **EA inputs stick** — after path/input rename, reattach EA and click **Reset** on inputs.
4. Repo `MQL5\*.mq5` edits do nothing until copied into the MetaEditor Experts folder and **F7**.

## Correct paths (portable MT5)

| What | Path |
|------|------|
| EA `.mq5` / `.ex5` | `C:\Program Files\MetaTrader 5\MQL5\Experts\MyExperts\Hermes\` |
| Controller DLL | `C:\Program Files\MetaTrader 5\MQL5\Libraries\HermesWpfGuiController.dll` |
| WPF UI DLL (versioned) | `D:\Programming\AI_Agents\Hermes\Hermes.MT5\WpfGuiControllerTest\WpfTestApp\bin\Release\ui_vN\HermesWpfTerminalUiN.dll` |
| Repo EA source | `Hermes.MT5\WpfGuiControllerTest\MQL5\HermesWpfGuiControllerTest.mq5` |

**Do not** deploy only to `%AppData%\MetaQuotes\Terminal\...\MQL5\Experts\` — this install does not use that tree for the Hermes EA.

## Deploy checklist

```powershell
cd Hermes.MT5\WpfGuiControllerTest\WpfTestApp
dotnet build -c Release
# copy net48\HermesWpfTerminalUiN.dll → bin\Release\ui_vN\

cd ..\WpfGuiController
dotnet build -c Release

cd ..
.\Deploy-To-MT5.ps1
```

Then MetaEditor: reopen mq5 → **F7** → remove EA from chart → attach → **Reset** inputs.

Window titles and `txtBuildVersion` must show `BuildInfo.Version` (e.g. `v26`) to confirm the new UI DLL loaded.

## Resize grips

Main terminal, Settings, and Trading Sessions use `ResizeMode="CanResizeWithGrip"` (dots in bottom-right corner).
